off

# child = run every warehouse query in its own child process, so the 45s
#         DUCKDB_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS can actually KILL a runaway query (in-process
#         it only frees the waiting user; the query keeps burning CPU and holds
#         its concurrency permit for its real duration). Also contains a DuckDB
#         OOM or native crash to one runner instead of the whole API.
# off   = in-process execution (today's behaviour).
#
# Applies to the BACKEND app only — see the workflow header for why the
# jobs-worker is deliberately left in-process.
#
# Validate after flipping to `child`: look for the log line
# "Child-process query runner ACTIVE". Its absence means the runner silently
# degraded to in-process and the flip achieved nothing.
